From ud66c79831f7be949 at groups.google.com  Sun Oct 29 21:31:42 2017
From: ud66c79831f7be949 at groups.google.com (Ana-Maria Mocanu)
Date: Sun, 29 Oct 2017 21:31:42 +0000
Subject: Shiny set of dashboards on shinyapps.io
Message-ID: <v2Fa7m66iEQ.uknGynszCQAJ@shinyapps-users.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/shinyapps-users/c/v2Fa7m66iEQ/m/uknGynszCQAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Hi everyone.

We are implementing a set of dashboards for a client and I am trying to understand what the best tool would be for it.
They don't have a massive budget, so a BI tool is not an option.

My options would be Plotly Dash and Shiny, but I would probably prefer Shiny because I used it several times before. I would go with the professional plan and embed it to our client's portal.

My questions deploying the dashboard on shinyapps.io <http://shinyapps.io> would be:
- can I set rights on what people can see? e.g. tab-level view permissions?
- can I set up an unlimited number of users (consumers, not devs)?
- I can see that one account can be shared with many developers, however, can you set up developers per dashboard?

Many thanks for the help!

Ana

From u299a5089d6c6c523 at groups.google.com  Mon Oct 30 14:28:33 2017
From: u299a5089d6c6c523 at groups.google.com (Joshua Spiewak)
Date: Mon, 30 Oct 2017 14:28:33 +0000
Subject: Re: Shiny set of dashboards on shinyapps.io
Message-ID: <v2Fa7m66iEQ.AY1F7_hqCQAJ@shinyapps-users.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <v2Fa7m66iEQ.uknGynszCQAJ@shinyapps-users.groups.google.com>
References: <v2Fa7m66iEQ.uknGynszCQAJ@shinyapps-users.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/shinyapps-users/c/v2Fa7m66iEQ/m/AY1F7_hqCQAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

1) Within a given application, you would need to implement per-user restrictions.
2) An unlimited number of viewers may be added to private applications
3) An account is limited to 25 members. They have full rights to the account, with the exception of managing billing and account members.

You might want to follow up on the new Shiny community site <https://community.rstudio.com/c/shiny> as some aspects of your questions are more generic to Shiny than hosting on shinyapps.io <http://shinyapps.io>

Hope that helps!

